      </dl>
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
      To configure a DASD device by adding a udev rule, complete the following steps:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Take the following sample udev rule <code>41-dasd-eckd-0.0.4444.rules</code>:
      <CodeBlock code={"ACTION==\"add\", SUBSYSTEM==\"ccw\", KERNEL==\"0.0.4444\", DRIVER==\"dasd-eckd\", GOTO=\"cfg_dasd_eckd_0.0.4444\"\nACTION==\"add\", SUBSYSTEM==\"drivers\", KERNEL==\"dasd-eckd\", TEST==\"[ccw/0.0.4444]\", GOTO=\"cfg_dasd_eckd_0.0.4444\"\nGOTO=\"end_dasd_eckd_0.0.4444\"\n\nLABEL=\"cfg_dasd_eckd_0.0.4444\"\nATTR{[ccw/0.0.4444]online}=\"1\"\n\nLABEL=\"end_dasd_eckd_0.0.4444\""} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Convert the rule to Base64 encoded by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ base64 /path/to/file/"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Copy the following MCO sample profile into a YAML file:
